Fix a finite abelian group $G$. If $A\subset B$, the \emph{relative density} of $A$ in $B$ is the ratio $|A|/|B|$. If $X\subset G$, the density of $X$ in $G$ is denoted by $\mu(X) := |X|/|G|$. We write $\m{X}$ for the normalized indicator function $\m{X} = \mu(X)^{-1}\ind{X}$. 

For $f, g:G\to \ensuremath{\mathbf{C}}$, we use the normalizations 
\begin{equation*}
\inner{f}{g} := \frac{1}{|G|} \sum_{x\in G} f(x) \overline{g(x)} \quad \text{and}\quad f * g (x) := \frac{1}{|G|} \sum_{y\in G} f(y) {g(x-y)},
\end{equation*}
