\end{equation*}
so that $B'$ is $(2^{-270}\alpha)$-sheltered by $B$, provided that $c$ is sufficiently small (see \cite{Bloomthesis} for the definition of `sheltered' in this context). We see in a similar way that $B''$ has the required amount of shelter. Finally, if $x\in B''$ and $\gamma' \in \langle \widetilde{\Gamma}\rangle$, say $\gamma' = \sum_{\gamma\in \Gamma} \varepsilon_{\gamma}\gamma$ with $ \varepsilon_{\gamma}\in \{-1, 0, 1\}$, we have 
\begin{equation*}
